# AI News Aggregator - Project Rules

## Architecture
- `main.py` is CLI entry point only - no business logic
- `collectors/` handles data fetching from external sources
- `processor/` handles LLM summarization, classification, dedup
- `outputs/` handles writing to Notion, web, markdown, push notifications
- `storage/` handles SQLite persistence

## Coding Conventions
- Python 3.10+, type hints required
- Single file MUST NOT exceed 500 lines
- Single function MUST NOT exceed 50 lines
- All HTTP requests MUST use proxy from config (http://172.24.12.140:18888)
- All API keys come from `.env` file, referenced in `config.yaml` as `${VAR_NAME}`
- Use `httpx` for HTTP requests (async support + proxy friendly)
- Use `logging` module, not print()

## Config Pattern
- `config.yaml`: data source definitions, output settings, LLM config
- `.env`: secrets (API keys, tokens) - NEVER commit
- All collectors read from `config.yaml`, secrets resolved from environment

## When Adding New Data Source
1. Create `collectors/new_source_collector.py` inheriting `BaseCollector`
2. Add source config section in `config.yaml`
3. Register collector in `main.py`

## When Adding New Output
1. Create `outputs/new_output.py` inheriting base output interface
2. Add output config section in `config.yaml`
3. Register output in `main.py`

## Commit Messages
- Use English for all commit messages
- Short imperative style: "Add YouTube collector", "Fix dedup logic"
